{"ref":"BDB, סֶ֫רֶן","hw":"סֶ֫רֶן","html":"I. <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">סֶ֫רֶן</span></big><sub>21</sub><big>]</big>  <strong>n.m. tyrant, lord (</strong>Philist. loan-word<strong>)</strong>;—pl. abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">הַסְּרָנִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 16:30\" href=\"/Judges.16.30\">Ju 16:30</a> + 2 times; cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">סַרְנֵי</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 3:3\" href=\"/Judges.3.3\">Ju 3:3</a> + 16 times; sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">סַרְנֵיכֶם</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 6:4\" href=\"/I_Samuel.6.4\">1 S 6:4</a>;—only of <em>tyrants, lords</em> of the Philistines, five in no. <a data-ref=\"Judges 3:3\" href=\"/Judges.3.3\">Ju 3:3</a> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 13:3\" href=\"/Joshua.13.3\">Jos 13:3</a> (D), <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 6:16\" href=\"/I_Samuel.6.16\">1 S 6:16</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 6:18\" href=\"/I_Samuel.6.18\">18</a> cf. v <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 6:4\" href=\"/I_Samuel.6.4\">4</a>, i.e. appar., one ruling each of the five cities (named <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 6:17\" href=\"/I_Samuel.6.17\">1 S 6:17</a>); without the numeral <a data-ref=\"Judges 16:5\" href=\"/Judges.16.5\">Ju 16:5</a> + 6 times <a data-ref=\"Judges 16\" href=\"/Judges.16\">Ju 16</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 5:8\" href=\"/I_Samuel.5.8\">1 S 5:8</a> + 7 times 1 S, + <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 12:20\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.12.20\">1 Ch 12:20</a> (Baer Ginsb; v <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 12:19\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.12.19\">19</a> van d. H.).","next":"BDB, סֶ֫רֶן²","prev":"BDB, סָרִיס"}